# Testing Patterns & Conventions

## CRITICAL: Read Code Before Writing Tests

**Follow the "DEBUG FIRST" approach from the careful-fixes rule:**
- Read implementation before writing tests
- Trace actual behavior, not assumed behavior
- Never write tests based on naming assumptions (e.g., "hide" button might remove, not toggle)

## Backend Testing (Python/Pytest)
- Place in [tests/](mdc:backend/tests/), use `test_` prefix
- FastAPI TestClient for endpoints, test success/error scenarios
- Test database: isolation, CRUD operations
- Service tests: mock dependencies, test edge cases
- Target 80%+ coverage (MVP)

## Frontend Testing (React/Jest)
- React Testing Library for components, test user interactions
- Hook tests with renderHook, mock external dependencies
- Service tests: mock API calls, test error handling
- Target 70%+ coverage (MVP)

## Integration Testing
- API: complete request/response cycles, auth validation
- E2E: Playwright for critical workflows
- Place E2E in [tests/e2e/](mdc:frontend/tests/e2e/)

## Test Data & Fixtures
- Use factories for test data, keep minimal
- Mock external APIs, file operations
- Clean up after tests

## Test Quality
- Descriptive test names, test one thing per case
- Focus on critical business logic
- Test happy path and main error scenarios